# UI in this SPA

Tokens live in [`src/index.css`](src/index.css) `@theme`. Product metaphor is **서재** (personal library). No door / fridge / “책장을 연다” language.

Light default is **Soft Deckle** (`data-palette="deckle"`): zero-hue archival paper, near-black ink-only magnet, **Newsreader** display + **DM Sans** UI (SUIT Hangul fallback), **JetBrains Mono** for spine/archival labels. Near-flat radius (6–8px). Dark Soft Deckle is near-black paper (`#121214`). `/login` folio uses mono **AI BOOKSHELF**; the header wordmark has no Soft Deckle subtitle.

Settings theme palettes:

- **소프트 데클** / Soft Deckle (`deckle`): default above.
- **에디토리얼** / Editorial (`editorial`): Minimal Editorial — white ground, ink `#09090b`, Space Grotesk display + Inter UI, near-zero radius. Inter/Space Grotesk are allowed only under this palette.

Warm · B and 현무암 are retired from Settings (legacy `warm`/`basalt`/`kitchen` localStorage values migrate to `deckle`). Do not add header **AI** / celadon unless PRODUCT asks. Auth sheet follows **Auth Ladder** on login, and **Auth Recovery** on find / reset (header back icon → brief → email → primary → feedback → **또는** → Google). Use `auth-back-btn`, `auth-btn-*`, `auth-link-*` from [`src/index.css`](src/index.css). Full rules: [DESIGN.md](DESIGN.md) Auth sheet hierarchy. New centered confirms and notice sheets use the **Protocol Stamp Modal** (`.protocol-modal-*` + [`AppDialog`](src/components/AppDialog.tsx)), not pill `auth-btn-*` or browser `confirm()`.

Routes: `/` intro or library, `/login`, `/stick`, `/search`, `/dashboard`, `/notices`, `/settings`, `/upgrade`, `/terms`, `/privacy`, `/scrap/:id`. Intro is Soft Deckle / Editorial integrated hero demo (담기 → AI 분석 → 정리 → 서재) with in-page promo-film stage motion (no MP4). Hero CTA and header 로그인 both navigate to the dedicated `/login` page (reuses `AuthSheet` with `variant="page"` as an archival dossier card: Google first, then email form, browse guest; no scrim/close-X, redirects to `/` if already signed in); CTA copy is **내 서재로** / Enter my library.

Signed-in header: two nav tabs — **나의 서재** `/`, **서재 통계** `/dashboard` — plus a Find icon (**장서 탐색** / Explore library via `searchOpen`, also `Cmd/Ctrl+K` → `/search`), a personal notices bell (panel always links to `/notices`), and an account control (Google `avatar_url`/`picture` or ink User squircle) that opens `/settings`. Content columns are **base `min(100%, 88rem)`** for shelf, dashboard, search, notices, settings, legal, and upgrade (no 40rem content-column base). Exceptions: `/login`, scrap detail, and the Stick dock (`.stick-float-inner` stays `max-width: 40rem`). `/notices` uses icon-only `settings-arch-chip` mark-all / clear (IconTip + aria-label; no liquid-glass); unread rows get a stronger outline and ink title; read rows use `--color-muted` title. Search uses a Soft Deckle command bar with an attached **캘린더 필터** tray (range / single day / monthly archive → `from`/`to` URL params) and a post-search facet panel (media multi-select, result tags, date refine slider). Search empty (no scraps) reuses shelf template cards via [`EmptyTemplateHints`](src/components/EmptyTemplateHints.tsx) without seed/담기 CTAs; Look still says **페이지 탐색**.

Plan UI labels are always **Free / Middle / High** (DB ids `free` / `standard` / `premium`). Limits and gates live in [`src/lib/plans.ts`](src/lib/plans.ts). Compare matrix is [`/upgrade`](src/pages/Upgrade.tsx). Trial expiry keeps Stick open and routes classify attempts to `/upgrade`.

After session: search and list above, Stick dock below (send = **분류하기** / Classify). A new stick/paste/drop replaces an open classify draft. The single-draft classify review at `/stick` renders as [`Workbench`](src/components/Workbench.tsx): a 3-step mono rail (`workbenchStep1-3`) plus a CSS 3D book-cover preview, wrapping the same `DraftCard` fields with `hideActions`. Email sheet is Soft Deckle / Editorial paper. Settings follows **Settings Ladder** in [DESIGN.md](DESIGN.md): Soft Deckle archival section cards; language, Deckle/Editorial theme cards, light·system·dark, reading scale, storage (browse local / account reset; Middle+ sync stub); stub chips for profile/2FA show **준비 중** — no Markdown export, no Look switcher, no invented live backends.

Shelf layout is **Gallery** (default, 3:2 visual poster grid) or **List** (storage id `micro` via `mybrary.shelfLayout`, horizontal media rows with 3:2 thumbs, blurb, and tags) — no accordion layout. The shelf opens with a workbench strip (서재 워크벤치 + archival count + labeled List/Gallery segment). The type book carousel (spine) always renders its 8 fixed sections (전체/책갈피/메모/사진/영상/소리/링크/문서, zero-count included), uses `--font-mono` for section titles, lifts on hover, and goes sticky + compact on desktop scroll only (enter ~160px / exit ~72px hysteresis). On desktop (≥960px) selecting a List or Gallery card opens [`ShelfInspector`](src/components/ShelfInspector.tsx) as a right-hand panel instead of navigating; below that width the same tap goes straight to `/scrap/:id`.

`PageChrome` is `flex min-h-dvh flex-col` with `#main { flex: 1 0 auto }` so short content still pins `.site-footer` to the viewport bottom.

Copy: stick / peel / 나가기; composer send label is **분류하기**. Stick **+** matches header circular hover disks (no liquid-glass); `IconTip` supports `suppress` while menus are open. Storage usage strings use 페이지/pages. Look axis may still exist in prefs/CSS without a Settings control. No em-dashes. Empty operator fields: 표시 예정. Honor `prefers-reduced-motion`. Binding visuals: [DESIGN.md](DESIGN.md).
